  "Brazil": {
    "anthem": "Hino Nacional Brasileiro",
    "native": "Hino Nacional Brasileiro",
    "id": "br",
    "history": "Composed in 1831, it celebrates the independence and the beauty of the Brazilian landscape.",
    "funFact": "The lyrics are extremely formal and complex, containing many poetic inversions that even native speakers find difficult.",
    "lyrics": "I\nOuviram do Ipiranga as margens plácidas\nDe um povo heroico o brado retumbante,\nE o sol da liberdade, em raios fúlgidos,\nBrilhou no céu da pátria nesse instante.\n\nSe o penhor dessa igualdade\nConseguimos conquistar com braço forte,\nEm teu seio, ó liberdade,\nDesafia o nosso peito a própria morte!\n\nÓ Pátria amada,\nIdolatrada,\nSalve! Salve!\n\nBrasil, um sonho intenso, um raio vívido\nDe amor e de esperança à terra desce,\nSe em teu formoso céu, risonho e límpido,\nA imagem do Cruzeiro resplandece.\n\nGigante pela própria natureza,\nÉs belo, és forte, impávido colosso,\nE o teu futuro espelha essa grandeza.\n\nRefrão:\nTerra adorada,\nEntre outras mil,\nÉs tu, Brasil,\nÓ Pátria amada!\nDos filhos deste solo és mãe gentil,\nPátria amada, Brasil!\n\nII\nDeitado eternamente em berço esplêndido,\nAo som do mar e à luz do céu profundo,\nFulguras, ó Brasil, florão da América,\nIluminado ao sol do Novo Mundo!\n\nDo que a terra, mais garrida,\nTeus risonhos, lindos campos têm mais flores;\n\"Nossos bosques têm mais vida\",\n\"Nossa vida\" no teu seio \"mais amores.\" (*)\n\nÓ Pátria amada,\nIdolatrada,\nSalve! Salve!\n\nBrasil, de amor eterno seja símbolo\nO lábaro que ostentas estrelado,\nE diga o verde-louro dessa flâmula\n– \"Paz no futuro e glória no passado.\"\n\nMas, se ergues da justiça a clava forte,\nVerás que um filho teu não foge à luta,\nNem teme, quem te adora, a própria morte.\n\nRefrão",
    "translation": "I\nThe placid shores of the Ipiranga heard,\nthe resounding shout of a heroic people.\nAnd the sun of Liberty in shining beams,\nshone in the homeland's sky at that instant.\n\nIf the pledge[b] of this equality\nwe managed to conquer with strong arm,\nin thy bosom, O Freedom,\nour chest defieth death itself!\n\nO beloved,\nidolized homeland,\nHail, hail!\n\nBrazil, an intense dream, a vivid ray\nof love and hope to earth descendeth.\nIf in thy beautiful, smiling and limpid sky,\nthe image of the [Southern] Cross blazeth.\n\nGiant by thine own nature,\nThou art beautiful, strong, a fearless colossus,[c]\nAnd thy future mirrors that greatness\n\nChorus:\nAdored land\nAmongst a thousand others\nart thou, Brazil,\nO beloved homeland\nOf the sons of this ground\nThou art kind mother\nBeloved homeland, Brazil!\n\nII\nEternally lying on a splendid cradle,\nto the sound of the sea and in the light of the deep sky.\nThou flashest, o Brazil, crocket of America,\nilluminated by the sun of the New World.\n\nThan the most ostentatious land,\nthy smiling, beautiful meadows have more flowers.\n\"Our forests have more life,\"\n\"Our life\" in thy bosom \"more loves\".\n\nO beloved,\nidolized homeland,\nHail, hail!\n\nBrazil, of eternal love, may\nthe starry ensign which thou displayest be a symbol.\nAnd may the laurel-green of this pennon say:\n\"Peace in the future and glory in the past.\"\n\nBut if thou raisest the strong cudgel [d] of justice,\nthou shalt see that a son of thine fleeth not from battle,\nnor do those who love thee fear death itself[e].\n\nChorus",
    "ja_name": "ブラジル",
    "history_ja": "1831 年に作曲され、ブラジルの独立と美しい風景を讃えています。",
    "funFact_ja": "歌詞は非常に形式的かつ複雑で、ネイティブスピーカーでも難しい詩の倒置が多く含まれています。",
    "translation_ja": "I\nイピランガの穏やかな岸辺は聞いた\n英雄的な人々の響き渡る叫びを\nそして自由の太陽が輝く光線とともに\nその瞬間、祖国の空に輝いた\n\nもしこの平等の誓いを\n我らが強き腕で勝ち取ることができたなら\nおお自由よ、汝の懐の中で\n我らの胸は死そのものにも立ち向かう\n\nおお愛しき\n偶像化された祖国よ\n万歳、万歳！\n\nブラジルよ、激しい夢、鮮やかな光線\n愛と希望が地上に降り注ぐ\n汝の美しく微笑む澄み切った空に\n南十字星の姿が燃え輝くとき\n\n自らの本質によって巨大な者よ\n汝は美しく、強く、恐れを知らぬ巨人なり\nそして汝の未来はその偉大さを映し出す\n\nコーラス：\n愛されし大地よ\n数多ある国々の中でも\n汝はブラジル\nおお愛しき祖国よ\nこの地の息子たちにとって\n汝は慈悲深き母なり\n愛しき祖国、ブラジルよ！\n\nII\n燦然たる揺りかごに永遠に横たわり\n海の音と深い空の光の中で\nおおブラジルよ、汝は輝く、アメリカの宝石よ\n新世界の太陽に照らされて\n\n最も華やかな土地よりも\n汝の微笑む美しい草原には多くの花がある\n「我らの森はより多くの命を宿し」\n「我らの命」は汝の懐で「より多くを愛する」\n\nおお愛しき\n偶像化された祖国よ\n万歳、万歳！\n\n永遠の愛を持つブラジルよ、汝が掲げる\n星の旗が象徴となりますように\nそしてこの旗の月桂樹の緑が語らんことを\n「未来には平和を、過去には栄光を」\n\nしかし、もし汝が正義の強き棍棒を振り上げるなら\n汝の息子は戦いから逃げはせぬと知るだろう\n汝を愛する者は死そのものをも恐れぬのだから\n\nコーラス"
  },
